# STM32 Pan-Tilt Servo Control System

Hello! This repository contains a Pan-Tilt motor control project I developed to improve my skills in embedded systems and hardware programming. It serves as a strong foundation for my future robotics projects involving computer vision (OpenCV) autonomous target tracking, as well as for my TÜBİTAK and TEKNOFEST competition applications.

## 🚀 About the Project
In this project, rather than controlling a Pan-Tilt mechanism with basic blocking delays, I aimed to design a structured, responsive embedded system using core hardware features of the microcontroller, such as hardware timers, interrupts, and serial communication.

### 🛠️ Key Features & What I Implemented
- **Hardware PWM (TIM2):** Direct PWM signal generation via hardware timers for jitter-free and stable servo motor operation.
- **Smooth Acceleration (Ramping Algorithm):** Instead of jumping to target positions abruptly, the motors accelerate and decelerate smoothly using a dedicated TIM1 hardware timer interrupt running at regular intervals (10ms).
- **HMI Screen Control via UART:** Target positions and commands are sent from an external HMI display over UART, parsed in real time, and translated into servo movements.
- **UART Telemetry Output:** Real-time feedback including current velocity, target values, and system status is continuously transmitted over UART to a serial monitor.
- **Emergency Stop (EXTI):** An external push-button interrupt immediately locks the system into a safe state and halts all motion upon being triggered.

## 🧰 Hardware & Tools Used
- **Microcontroller:** STM32 Nucleo-F303RE
- **Actuators:** 2-Axis (Pan-Tilt) Servo Motor Mechanism
- **User Interface:** HMI Display (Communicating via UART)
- **Development Environment:** STM32CubeIDE
- **Library:** STM32 HAL (Hardware Abstraction Layer)
- **Language:** C

